{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"1st\" expr=\"0\"/>\n    <data id=\"max tries\" expr=\"3\"/>\n    <data id=\"$price\" expr=\"10\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"buy\" cond=\"$price &gt; 5\" target=\"b\">\n      <log label=\"first\" expr=\"1st\"/>\n    </transition>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":3,"notes":0,"total":4,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":125,"endColumn":18,"endLine":3,"startColumn":15,"startLine":3},"insertedContent":{"text":"v1st"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":335,"endColumn":35,"endLine":9,"startColumn":32,"startLine":9},"insertedContent":{"text":"v1st"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the variable to `v1st` here and in 1 reference"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":18,"endLine":3,"startColumn":15,"startLine":3}}}],"message":{"markdown":"identifier `1st` is not an XML NCName\n\n**Note:** SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`\n\n**Help:** a `<data id>` is both an XML ID and an ECMAScript variable name: use ASCII letters, digits, and `_`, starting with a letter\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"identifier `1st` is not an XML NCName"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":128,"start":125},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML003"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":9,"byteOffset":155,"endColumn":24,"endLine":4,"startColumn":15,"startLine":4},"insertedContent":{"text":"maxTries"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the variable to `maxTries`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":24,"endLine":4,"startColumn":15,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"identifier `max tries` is not an XML NCName\n\n**Note:** SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`\n\n**Help:** a `<data id>` is both an XML ID and an ECMAScript variable name: use ASCII letters, digits, and `_`, starting with a letter\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"identifier `max tries` is not an XML NCName"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":164,"start":155},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML003"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":6,"byteOffset":191,"endColumn":21,"endLine":5,"startColumn":15,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"price"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":6,"byteOffset":277,"endColumn":41,"endLine":8,"startColumn":35,"startLine":8},"insertedContent":{"text":"price"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the variable to `price` here and in 1 reference"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":21,"endLine":5,"startColumn":15,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"identifier `$price` is not an XML NCName\n\n**Note:** SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`\n\n**Help:** a `<data id>` is both an XML ID and an ECMAScript variable name: use ASCII letters, digits, and `_`, starting with a letter\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"identifier `$price` is not an XML NCName"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":197,"start":191},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML003"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":34,"endLine":9,"startColumn":33,"startLine":9}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: a number is immediately followed by a letter, `$`, or `_`\n\n**Note:** an expression that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated\n\n**Help:** separate the number from the name that follows it, or start the name with a letter\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: a number is immediately followed by a letter, `$`, or `_`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":337,"start":336},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `expr`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-not-ncname.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":35,"endLine":9,"startColumn":32,"startLine":9}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: rename the identifier to a valid NCName, for example replacing spaces and colons with `_`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML003` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#IDs","id":"SCXML003","name":"SCXML003","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an identifier is not an XML NCName"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.9.4: \"The SCXML Processor MAY reject documents containing syntactically ill-formed expressions at document load time, or it MAY wait and place 'error.execution' in the internal event queue at runtime when the expressions are evaluated.\" This toolchain takes the second option, so the document compiles and the expression raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated (a condition is then false and the rest of an executable-content block is skipped); this check runs only when the host supplies the data model's parse-only syntax capability (the native CLI links the ECMAScript and XPath checkers). Each finding names the offending source text and, where a repair is certain to parse, offers it: ECMAScript habits in XPath (`==` to `=`, `&&` to `and`, `||` to `or`, `!x` to `not(x)`, `length()` to `string-length()`), a stray `=` in ECMAScript (`x === = 3`), word operators, quoting, and more. The XPath data model has no script language, so a non-empty `<script>` is reported too"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: apply the suggested repair, or fix the syntax at the marked position following the finding's help; for XPath, use XPath 1.0 operators and functions (`=`, `and`, `or`, `not()`, `string-length()`, `count()`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML038` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ecma-profile","id":"SCXML038","name":"SCXML038","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an expression or script does not parse in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}